{"id":"f24a3f45-88c8-45e3-8033-0eacb3f092d0","object":"chat.completion","created":1784808226,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    payload = case['payload']\\n    wti = payload['word_token_indices']\\n    wl = payload['word_labels']\\n    tc = payload['token_count']\\n    if len(wti) != len(wl):\\n        return {\\\"error\\\": \\\"length mismatch\\\"}\\n    token_labels = [None] * tc\\n    for i, indices in enumerate(wti):\\n        label = wl[i]\\n        for idx in indices:\\n            if not (0 <= idx < tc):\\n                return {\\\"error\\\": \\\"out of range\\\"}\\n            if token_labels[idx] is not None:\\n                return {\\\"error\\\": \\\"overlap\\\"}\\n            token_labels[idx] = label\\n    for idx in range(tc):\\n        if token_labels[idx] is None:\\n            return {\\\"error\\\": \\\"uncovered\\\"}\\n    token_labels = [int(x) for x in token_labels]\\n    retained = [i for i, v in enumerate(token_labels) if v == 1]\\n    return {\\\"token_labels\\\": token_labels, \\\"retained_indices\\\": retained}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to parse the task. The user provides a fixture with cases. Each case has word_token_indices (list of lists, each inner list contains token indices for a word), word_labels (list of labels for each word, presumably 0 or 1), and token_count (total number of tokens). The objective: project word-level keep/drop labels onto subword spans and recover a faithful ordered token mask. Essentially, for each word, its label applies to all its token indices. Need to produce a token-level vector of labels (length token_count) where each token gets the label of the word it belongs to. Then return the full token-label vector and retained indices (indices where label == 1). Also validate: every word must have a label (already given), token indices must be within range (0 to token_count-1), no overlapping token